#: src/Admin/PrivacyIntegration.php:544
msgid "Edge-decided language redirect"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/PrivacyIntegration.php:545
msgid "When this site is deployed behind an edge platform (Cloudflare, Vercel, Netlify), an edge worker may inspect the country code provided by the platform and forward a chosen language slug to the origin via the X-PerfLocale-Lang request header or a perflocale_edge_lang cookie. The cookie, when set, contains only the language slug (for example \"en\", \"fr\") - no IP address, no personal data. The country lookup happens at the edge; this plugin does not transmit your IP address to a third-party API for this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/PrivacyIntegration.php:554
#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:3431
#: src/Enum/SourceType.php:64
msgid "Machine translation"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: configured machine-translation provider name
#: src/Admin/PrivacyIntegration.php:557
#, php-format
msgid "Site administrators may send post, page, or string content to %s for machine translation. This is triggered by site staff, not by end visitors, and sends the content to the provider&rsquo;s API for the sole purpose of returning a translated version. Visit your provider&rsquo;s data-processing documentation for details on their retention and processing guarantees."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/PrivacyIntegration.php:560
msgid "Text you send for machine translation is transmitted to the provider you configured. PerfLocale keeps only the translated result: saved on the post, or held with a Content ReSync update as described below. Content ReSync sends the new or changed parts of a translation only when its \"Changed and new parts\" setting is set to machine translate them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/PrivacyIntegration.php:567
msgid "With each part Content ReSync machine translates, text around it is also sent as context to providers that accept it: the neighbouring parts or its section of the same post, and its earlier translation. An outdated string is sent with its current translation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/PrivacyIntegration.php:575
msgid "When site staff update translations from their source posts with Content ReSync, PerfLocale stores copies of post text in its own database tables: the version of each source post a translation was last updated from, proposed updates waiting for review, and the text an applied update replaced, so that the update can be undone. These copies contain whatever the posts contain, which can include personal data. Each update also records which user started it and which user decided it; these records are exported and erased with Tools &rarr; Export Personal Data and Erase Personal Data."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/PrivacyIntegration.php:579
msgid "A proposed update waits until a reviewer applies or rejects it, a newer update replaces it, its source post is permanently deleted, its translation is trashed or deleted, or its language is removed. Stored copies of a source post are removed after the post is permanently deleted. A decided update is removed 90 days after the decision, with the text it replaced, except the latest applied update of each translation, which is kept while the translation exists. A source version that no update uses is removed after 90 days without use. Machine translation results of a run that stopped before saving expire after one day, and WordPress removes expired entries in its daily clean-up. When the plugin is deleted, these copies are removed only if \"Delete all plugin data when uninstalling\" is turned on under PerfLocale &rarr; Settings &rarr; Advanced; otherwise they stay in the database for a reinstall."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/PrivacyIntegration.php:587
msgid "Admin user preferences"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/PrivacyIntegration.php:588
msgid "For registered users with access to the WordPress admin area, PerfLocale stores a small set of UI preferences against your user profile (which language columns you have hidden on the Strings and Translations admin tables, and how many rows you display per page). These are not shared with anyone, are exported via Tools &rarr; Export Personal Data, and are deleted via Tools &rarr; Erase Personal Data or automatic cleanup when your user account is removed."
msgstr ""

